WEBVTT

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.040
Hey!

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.930
How long have you been there!?

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.080
The door was locked-

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.540
Give me back that hoodie I lent you.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.660
You gave it to me, so it's mine now.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.320
I'm never giving it back.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:38.230
So there!

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.790
You're such a tightwad.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.010
Fine then.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:43.720
Regsuuld Stagga

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.600
Stay still for a second.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.000
You always have to make things more difficult.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:02.180
Damn, the magic is getting in the way.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.560
What if you undo the spell for a second?

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.640
Oh, that's smart!

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:10.000
They're releas-

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.160
You're too gullible.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:16.640
What's with you?

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:17.320
Stupid orc!

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:18.140
You're such a-

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:33.820
Wasn't that messed up?

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:34.550
Yeah...

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.440
It was just an old hoodie. Just let her have it.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:41.640
She just borrowed my stuff and never gave it back.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:47.990
I never got the hoodie back, but she gave me this.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:51.200
But I could never wear something this gaudy.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:51.930
Yeah.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:54.230
If only we knew a girl who-

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:54.980
Oh.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:01:59.050
So...

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.640
Why am I in this again?

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.510
That looks great!

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.360
Really, you think so?

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.790
She used to dress like that all the time.

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:10.800
I kind of miss-

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.350
To think I'd feel nostagic over that other world.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:21.020
This has to be crazy expensive, right?

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.670
Is that right?

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:24.920
Maybe I should try it on, afterall.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:25.760
Why!?

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:42.850
Refrain keshita kioku rewrite

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:42.850
Refrain those erased memories, rewrite​

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:48.570
Monogatari no tsune ga ima miseru kotoba de

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:48.570
With the words that give a glimpse of the story

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.780
Don't end this, won't change it​

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.530
Dou shitatte kaerarenai

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.530
Can't change it, no matter what you do

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:57.030
Mokuteki wo wasurenaideite

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:57.030
Don't forget your goal​

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.410
Dare ga kimetan da

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.410
Who decides

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.960
Sonna ikikata rashikunai yo

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.960
the way we should and shouldn't live?

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.130
Yaritai koto tsuranuku chikara

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.130
The strength to do what you want to do​

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.380
Sore koso ga tsuyosa datte

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.380
That's what really makes you strong​ ​

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:14.930
Wakatteiru kara

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:14.930
I know that's the truth

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.840
I believe in what I've done​

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.300
No reason to go back again​

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.220
Ayunde kita hibi wo

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.220
The meaning of nostalgia

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.850
Natsukashimu imi wo

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.850
For those days I walked​

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.640
Easy losing memories​

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.770
I'm struggling now to overcome​

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.980
Akirameru koto wa nai

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.980
I will never give up​

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.570
Saigo made

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.570
Until the end​

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.450
Get down, let's get down​

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:41.120
Kokoro no hikari wo oboeteru uchi ni

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:41.120
While I still remember the light in my heart​

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.290
Trust yourself

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.500
Don't deny

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.920
Save yourself

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.460
Don't forget

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:59.560
So, after a rigorous selection process...

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:04.610
My otherworld transfer
bonus the translation skill...

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:08.330
Will be officially called "Wild Talker".

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.180
Takafumi's suggestion is the winner.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.070
Y-Yay...

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:13.210
H-Hooray...

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.440
Thank god we avoided Uncle's idea.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:18.160
Uncle's idea had to go, no question.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:22.790
By the way, this has nothing to do with Wild Talker, but...

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:23.130
Ah...

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.540
I almost forgot!

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:30.490
Sorry, I gotta go.
I'm supposed to do some stuff at college today!

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.110
Are they holding a lecture today?

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:35.410
Well, Let's just say it's a minor errand.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:39.920
Later!

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.670
See this?
Go here, and...

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:51.260
...VOILÀ!

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:52.610
See!?

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:56.220
Just lead them in at the right angle, and they'll fall and die.

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:58.490
Sure...

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:00.490
By the way, uncle, what is-

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:02.830
It's a Mega Drive.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:05.590
I bought it with channel revenue earned so far.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:13.970
Well, I'll have you know all that gaming saved the day when I was in the otherworld.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.630
Icras elran.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:20.110
There was this village under attack from a horde of goblins...

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:24.640
I was working with another team of adventurers to fend them off.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.010
Working with them!?

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.010
Oh...
It's a bit after that...

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.010
Fastforward... Fastforward...

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.680
S-stay back... please...

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.680
Damn,
it's some kind of freak monster goblin!

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:39.680
Alicia, run!

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:43.140
I'm not a goblin.

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:47.610
I'm not an orc.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.360
Wait. I know you...

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.810
from Winter Festival!

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.860
Ahh, when I entered the village, everyone grouped up on me.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:55.010
I'm not an orc.

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:55.430
You were there at that time?

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.920
Ah, Yes. But we also met you on our way back.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.460
Swordsman
Edgar

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.460
Holy Mage
Alicia

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.460
Martial Artist
Raiga

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.640
What? Working together?

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:07.220
Silly, that dude's clearly gonna side with the goblins!

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:08.430
Yes...
Even if heisn't an orc,

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.850
he's a creature that's borderline monster.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:11.970
Um, excuse me!

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:18.250
The village of Dold is up ahead. We accepted a request to defend them from a horde of goblins, but-

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:18.760
All right.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:20.880
Huh?

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:23.190
Would you be willing to help us!?

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:24.890
Yeah, sure. I'm in.

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:26.920
Yes!

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:37.280
How are there so many of 'em!?

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.280
This wasn't what they told us!

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:40.500
Don't worry.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:44.400
I've got a cunning plan.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:45.650
I got this.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:49.850
Hey!!

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:51.010
Come straight at me!

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.570
Straight!

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:54.220
Straight!

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:00.780
Uncle...

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:01.870
Now hold on.

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:04.980
Yes, for some reason the "lure into pitfall" strat didn't work out, but...

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.370
"For some reason", huh!?

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:06.740
It's hard to land it on enemies but...

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:13.830
When you do a dash-jump and hit the attack button in Golden Axe, you do this big-damage move called a "downward thrust."

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:20.560
Whoa!

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:21.570
What a leap!

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:22.640
Is that wind magic!?

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:30.100
...You're whiffing every strike, uncle...

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:33.230
Yeah, I told you it was hard to land...

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:51.810
...and that's how I applied my Golden Axe techniques to fend off an entire goblin horde.

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:53.590
Liar!

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:58.200
Not a single thing from Golden Axe was remotely helpful there!
In fact, it made things harder for you!

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:00.790
...Takafumi...

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:02.010
As you saw right there,

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:05.860
my SEGA gaming paid off big-time in my life...!!

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:09.400
It doesn't help SEGA's image any when you defend the brand with paper-thin reasoning. Just stop!

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:14.600
...after that, we headed to town to claim our reward.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.940
Dude, that rocked!

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:18.680
Are you sure you're okay with going foursies on this?

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:23.490
Yes, the last thing I want is to get on your bad side by taking more than my fair share, then get mobbed again for it later.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:26.170
Wow, Edgar actually laughed!

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:27.410
You're a real funny guy!

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:27.590
...Uncle!

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:30.430
You did have friends!
They're right there!

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.460
Hey...

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:40.260
...You rebuilt the barrier in Luvaldram, right?

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.030
You... saw that?

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.010
Did you tell anyone?

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.830
No one would believe me if I did...

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:55.070
You look...

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:58.030
Frankly, you look scary, but still.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:01.690
You're almost like a legendary hero...

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:01.680
Icuras cuora!

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:05.760
Wha-!?

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:07.390
I trusted you...

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:08.360
Icuras cuora.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:14.510
So...

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:16.630
That was the last time you saw them?

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:18.030
No, I met them again.

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:24.480
Thinking back, there was this time in the otherworld where a language suddenly clicked with me.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:25.930
Wh... What kind of creature...?

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:30.810
I was wondering if maybe that was Wild Talker kicking in.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:34.250
I bless you both with sacred power!

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:35.300
Those are humans!!

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:38.400
Stop him from charging up!

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:39.860
His barrier's impenetrable!!

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:40.830
Huh, wait...

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:43.890
Oh, right... Let's fast forward...

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.330
Y- You're the guy...

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:52.240
...who got mobbed by the whole village at the winter passage thanksgiving and fought us all off...

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:53.170
Yeah.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.280
I'm not an orc.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.890
Why am I getting déjà vu from this...?

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:59.870
It's the trio that uncle fought together with.
Then he erased their memories...

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:02.010
I'm Raiga

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.030
My name's Alicia.

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:04.290
...Edgar.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.290
I'm Kuroki Tenma.

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:07.440
Nice to meet you.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:10.000
He gave another bogus alias...
Damn, that one's rad...

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:08.890
Kuroki.

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:11.220
So what brings you guys out this way?

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:15.210
...See that old shrine?
It's become a monster lair.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:19.870
We took on a quest from Shaleg to slay it, but we haven't been a match for it so far.

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:21.640
What kind of monster is it?

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:25.500
Well um... It's called a Stabber beast...
Do you know what a "hedgehog" is?

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:29.230
It's a monster that's basically one of those, but as tall as a human.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.230
That... Sounds like Soni-

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:34.670
It can tighten its defenses by curling into a ball too.
We're kinda stumped on how to slay it...

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:36.560
D-Don't slay it!

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:37.560
Huh?

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:40.840
"Why do monsters attack people?"

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:46.670
If we could find out the reason for it,
we might not have to fight at all!

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:48.720
Huh? The reason?

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:51.950
Are you stupid!?
Do you think we have the time to debate this crap!?

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:53.470
Ah! There it is!

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:53.940
Huh!?

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:55.250
Sonic!

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:04.550
...who are you?

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.040
As you can see,

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:10.440
hedgehogs in this world bear no resemblance whatsoever to the ones on Earth...

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.430
They're not blue, and they move slowly.

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:15.310
Uh... are you sure about that...?

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:18.830
Yeah, I know a pretty good deal about hedgehogs...

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:21.930
Monster...

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:24.310
Are humans encroaching on your territory?

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:26.820
Are humans spoiling your way of life?

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:29.630
Why do you attack humans!?

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:32.210
Do you have babies that make you extra vigilant?

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.330
Have humans killed your family!?

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.470
Please! Answer me!

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:36.330
I...

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:37.700
I...

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:39.700
...don't want to kill you!!

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:43.170
I... I understand it...!

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:44.820
Wha-!?

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:47.490
I understand what the stabber beast is saying!!

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:50.620
I don't like human meat.

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.190
Really? Then why...?

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.720
It amuses me to stab humans and torture them.

00:11:56.670 --> 00:11:58.010
Uh...

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:00.690
It pleases me to hear the screams of humans in their death throes.

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:04.110
I like to kill humans in the most painful way possible-

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:07.620
Baraibhut folg bastohl.

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:21.610
Oh...

00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:23.920
...And that's how I managed to achieve a dialogue...

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:30.340
Maybe Wild Talker's activation requirement is "a strong, earnest desire to have dialogue with the target."

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:32.340
Uh... yeah. Sure...

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:35.030
Boy, when uncle decides to fight, he shows zero mercy...

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.950
Dude. That was nuts...

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:40.610
What did the monster say?

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:42.520
Well, anyway...

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:47.460
I heard there was a hero around these parts.
Do you guys know anything about that?

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:49.120
A hero!?

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.320
Oh yeah, Elf-san mentioned that before...

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:58.420
Fujimiya forgot her smartphone!
I gotta get it to her asap!

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.890
Huh...?
...can't this wait until tomorrow?

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:05.450
Nowadays, when people leave the house without their smartphone,
it's like playing a game with no controller!

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.270
It's that bad!?
Crap we'd better hurry!

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:17.130
Flying in the sky feels great, huh, uncle!?

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:18.180
Sure does!

00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:21.490
But it gets real cold in the winter,
so let's stick to the train then!

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.000
So...

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:27.950
Where is that girl...?

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:28.380
Hm?

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:31.750
Ah.

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:35.600
Oh, hey.
Fujimiya-san's over there.

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:43.760
Takafumi...

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.170
I'm just going to watch.
Resolve it for yourself.

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:48.270
I get you.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:50.200
I...

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:52.200
I'm gonna make sure he's all right for her.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.200
That's what friends do.

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:55.960
Friends, huh...?

00:13:57.400 --> 00:13:59.130
Just put me down somewhere inconspicuous.

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:00.000
Hold up.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:03.930
I'll hook you up with a few little spirit blessings.

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:05.460
Ah, spirits? Hey, guys!

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:13.930
This is Shibazaki, the guy from the Youtube channel "Uncle From Another World"!

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:18.200
There, that should give you acess to all the magic I can use.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:19.520
Temporarily.

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:21.850
Wow.
Thanks, uncle!

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:23.540
Takafumi...

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:28.160
If he does turn out to be an all right guy for her,
what will you do then?

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:30.050
If he's an all right guy...

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.630
...then it's not my place to butt in.

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:33.350
All right.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:34.380
And if he's trash, I'll erase him.

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:34.900
Whoa, uh...

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:35.760
His memories, I mean.

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:37.980
Oh...
Okay...

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.900
C'mon, C'mooon!

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:43.180
I wanna go to the beach and spend the night!

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:44.440
...we're not going.

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:48.150
Aww, why not? We went to a hot spring last year!

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:52.360
I'm busy this year! For one thing, when we went to the hot spring you wouldn't let me sleep at all-

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:52.380
Fujimiya.

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:00.450
Whoa, what are you doing here!?

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:02.880
Huuhh?
Whozzis?

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.560
You forgot your smartphone.

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:06.920
Oh...
Uh, thanks...

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:10.520
...uh?

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:11.560
What?

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:12.520
Chiaki-kun?

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:16.520
Wha-?

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:19.120
It's me, Takafumi!
Don't you remember me?

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:29.460
T...

00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:31.690
Takafumi-niichan!?

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:32.760
Mhm!

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:34.660
Oh my gooosh! It's been years!

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.550
Wow, you're so big now!
I didn't recognize you at all!

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:39.910
I had a growth spurt in highschool...!

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:43.760
You've grown pretty big yourself, Chiaki-kun.
You're in, what... the forth grade now?

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:44.820
Yup!

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:48.460
<i>Oh yeah!
I'm visiting college with Sumi-nee to do a Youtube recording!</i>

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.840
Oh! Uncle...

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:51.530
<i>Oh yeah? You're a Youtuber Chiaki-kun? That's great!</i>

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:51.830
Wow...

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:56.620
<i>Yup! Heh heh heh... Sometimes I get a whole fifty views!</i>

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:52.950
Your little brother?

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:57.690
I heard kids these days grow up fast, but this takes the cake...

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:59.820
<i>Wow, fifty views! That's bigger than your whole class!</i>

00:15:57.690 --> 00:15:59.690
Oh right! Hey, Chiaki!

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:03.530
See this man?
This is the Youtuber I was telling you about!

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:07.730
Really!?

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:08.920
Ahem...

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:13.650
Hello...

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:17.640
I run the channel Uncle From Another World.
I'm the uncle...!

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:19.280
...uh, who...!?

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:23.430
So do you like,
play video games and stuff?

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:24.640
Ah, yes.

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:27.800
I once played Guardian Heroes on the SEGA saturn...

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:29.590
SE-? Never heard of it.

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:34.920
...Do other Youtubers play that game?

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:36.060
Uh... Yeah.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:39.300
It gets featured a bit on Youtube channels famous for game playing...

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:45.840
<i>Oh, also, um... I don't know if it was the GH thing or what, but there was this one time my video got featured on a well-known gaming channel on Youtube...</i>

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:43.270
...You know, you were acting really on edge at first.

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:44.610
What was that?

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:45.830
Chiaki-kun...

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.830
I couldn't tell from a distance, but...

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:51.120
I thought maybe it was your boyfriend.

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:51.960
Huh!?

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:53.670
I don't have a boyfriend!

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:55.970
I mean, it wouldn't surprise me if you did.

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:57.240
You're so cute...

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:57.780
Cu-!?

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:05.720
...Wait, hold on.
Were you about to pick a fight with my "boyfriend"?

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:07.290
Look...

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:12.000
I thought maybe you'd fallen for the sweet-talk from some bad-news punk, and I kinda got ahead of myself...

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:16.890
<i>Ah! You can check out my videos on your phone! Look up "Uncle From Another World," and...</i>

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.450
Like hell I would. Stupid.

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:19.590
What if that really had been some bad-news punk? Could you have even fought him?

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:19.500
<i>Uhhh... No thanks, that's, like, giga-weak...</i>

00:17:19.590 --> 00:17:21.590
Well, for that...

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:23.490
Light spirit...

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:25.420
No...

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:27.420
More flashy.

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:29.000
Lightscreen camouflage.

00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:32.130
Huh? W-

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:33.890
I'm turning invisible here...

00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:35.220
Phantom vision.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:41.610
...a hologram...?

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:44.810
And mobility enshroud... is already active!

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:49.340
<i>Wouldn't it make for a better video if you...</i>

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:03.600
As you can see, I borrowed a little magic from uncle,
so I probably could've handled myself if it came to a fight.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.640
You can loan out and borrow magic...!?

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:08.810
And you seem crazy good at it already.
Is that just me?

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:09.780
Well.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:35.190
I've spent a lot of time thinking about how I'd subdue groups of enemies if we had magic in the modern day. The biggest weakness of magic incantation is time, you know? It doesn't matter how powerful your spell is if you get merced before you can finish casting it. So I've had this idea for a while that for basic spirit magic, as long as you envision the effect and voice it in the shortest possible terms, you can abbreviate the whole "spirit of X, do Y" thing. And voila - when I tried it out, it worked like a charm.

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:36.580
No, I don't know.

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:41.300
I knew you liked reading those types of light novels, but I didn't think it went that deep...

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.780
No, even before then.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:47.530
You know,

00:18:47.530 --> 00:18:50.050
this happened back in grade school too.

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:51.120
What did?

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:55.370
You stepped in when I was getting
ganged up on by older kids.

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:57.190
Oh, yeah...!

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:59.190
They'd shoved you to the ground, right?

00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:00.140
No?

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.000
They didn't shove me.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:04.080
Wait, really?

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:07.190
There's an easy way to check.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:09.920
Memory replay.

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:15.620
Hey! This place is for sixth-graders!

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:20.160
Oh yeah? If you're that big,
maybe you should act like it.

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:24.480
Someone here is whining like a baby,
and it sure isn't me...

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:27.730
Sh- Shut up, piggy!

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:31.250
It hurts! It hurts real bad here!

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:33.250
Moriyan! Moriyan, are you okay!?

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:35.890
Bweehee-hee... Oww. Ouchie.

00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:37.920
Well, you hit me first!

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:40.790
Hi-yah! Hoh!

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:41.450
Hee...

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.140
A-are you okay, Sumika-chan!?

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:44.610
Huh!?
T...Takafumi...!?

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:47.310
What kind of a meanie pushes a girl!?

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:49.570
Ah!

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:53.130
They really did push you! Does it hurt!?

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:56.340
N... No... I'm okay, I'm okay...

00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:59.090
Are you hurt at all!?

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:00.900
No, really... I'm fine...

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:02.020
I could carry you!

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:04.960
Kinda feels like I was the aggressor there...

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:07.650
I completely misread the situation, huh...?

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:09.650
Well, yeah.

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:17.440
Still...

00:20:21.140 --> 00:20:22.950
I was flattered,

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:23.750
honest.

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:28.330
You really come to my rescue both then and now...!

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:31.060
Hee hee...

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:35.740
Fujumiii!?

00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:39.860
Sa-?

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:41.860
Wha- Wha- Wha-!?

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:43.820
Who in the world!?

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:52.480
...yes, hello there. I'm Takafumi Takaoka, a friend of Fujimiya's from grade school.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:54.950
Hmm-hmmm!
Takafumi, huh?

00:20:54.950 --> 00:21:00.100
I'm Sawae, and I've been friends with her since high school! People call me Sawa!

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:03.620
Say! Say! Say!

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:07.220
Fujimo's gotten way cuter in the past six months, right?

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:11.420
You'd better watch out, orrr...

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:19.680
You don't say! Who is it!
You should introduce me!

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:22.180
G... Gosh, this is so sudden!

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:26.450
Hey, cut it out!
What are you going to do with my friend's number!?

00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:30.880
Oh, nothing.

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:34.420
Not getting the number and not doing anything with it are basically the same...

00:21:34.420 --> 00:21:35.700
You're...

00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:38.810
...clearly the type that can't be
trusted with any amount of power...!

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:42.740
...look. All I'm saying is,
college guys are inhuman.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:43.930
They're bugs...

00:21:43.930 --> 00:21:45.190
You have to swat them down...

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:50.610
...or else they'll use hypnosis on you at a party and gaslight you into coming home with them...!

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:51.480
Stop treating ludicrously lopsided internet claims as the gospel truth!

00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:54.490
Oh, crud!

00:21:54.490 --> 00:21:56.570
I'm supposed to be looking after Chiaki!

00:21:56.570 --> 00:21:58.740
Sorry, Sawa. Gotta take my brother home.

00:21:58.740 --> 00:22:01.720
Oh! Uh, sure.
Later!

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:05.520
Who was that...?

00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:07.520
Are you okay, Fujimii?

00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:11.810
Dropped Chiaki off at home.

00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:16.020
Did we ever figure out what
triggers Wild Talker?

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:19.350
I think it might be "direct dialogue"
and "desperation."

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:23.000
So far, there hasn't been a single case
where it got triggered on a lark.

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:27.930
What about when he managed to converse with
the spirits in Japan right after making it back here?

00:22:27.980 --> 00:22:29.030
Oh, that...

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:34.370
Back then, Takafumi was holding some government office paperwork and giving off a seriously deadly vibe.

00:22:35.360 --> 00:22:41.140
I thought to myself, "Oh no. If I can't use magic here, I'm going to get abandoned and die in the street."

00:22:43.140 --> 00:22:45.360
You were going to cut him off, weren't you!?

00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:48.880
A... Anyway, how about that hero, uncle!?

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:51.830
Oh, right. That story wasn't done.

00:22:51.830 --> 00:22:54.260
Huh!? Wait-
There's a hero now!?

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:56.390
Not yet, but apparently, it's close.

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:58.390
Icuras elran.

00:22:58.680 --> 00:23:01.820
Remember Alicia's group?

00:23:01.820 --> 00:23:03.980
The trio of adventurers who uncle memory-wiped...

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:06.100
They seem to know about it...

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:11.410
I heard there was a hero around these parts.

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:13.020
Do you guys know anything about that?

00:23:13.020 --> 00:23:15.010
Oh, that? Actually...

00:23:14.280 --> 00:23:15.010
Ahem!

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:19.090
Edgar, lemme see that real quick?

00:23:19.090 --> 00:23:20.860
Why?

00:23:20.860 --> 00:23:22.340
Just do it!

00:23:23.930 --> 00:23:25.530
Hup...

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:27.530
Hrgh...

00:23:30.370 --> 00:23:33.380
I am the hero chosen by fate...

00:23:33.380 --> 00:23:37.130
...The Shining Crusader...

00:23:37.130 --> 00:23:40.380
Alicia Edelcia...!
